1
00:02:06,959 --> 00:02:08,800
One seven two nine

2
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,159
Five seven two two

3
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:15,759
Two one three three

4
00:02:17,159 --> 00:02:19,280
One nine five zero

5
00:02:20,479 --> 00:02:22,840
Three two five three

6
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,400
Jinlan.

7
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,520
You're here early too.

8
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,120
Perfect timing, I need to talk to you.

9
00:03:55,439 --> 00:03:57,000
Yesterday, I was just a step too late.

10
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,120
If I had come back five minutes earlier,

11
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:58,960
I could have caught you.

12
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,199
Actually, it's no big deal.

13
00:04:02,199 --> 00:04:03,199
It was just a file cover.

14
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,120
But file covers need to be locked up too.

15
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,080
The higher-ups don't care

16
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,240
whether it holds top secrets or toilet paper.

17
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,120
Never,

18
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:32,040
ever groundlessly suspect

19
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,480
your own comrades and brothers-in-arms.

20
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,680
Unless

21
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:38,040
you can produce ironclad evidence.

22
00:04:40,439 --> 00:04:41,879
I'm not mad.

23
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:43,240
I'm just here to make a profit.

24
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,120
Even a sow needs to be fattened up before slaughter.

25
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,519
Asking me for ten thousand right off the bat...

26
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,959
Do they take me for a fool?

27
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,279
Brother, if you handle the takeoff, you gotta handle the landing.

28
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,399
You can't lure me here to invest and leave me to fend for myself.

29
00:04:52,399 --> 00:04:53,079
Come in.

30
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,360
Have a seat.

31
00:05:02,199 --> 00:05:03,399
Absolutely not.

32
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,600
That's not what I meant.

33
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,360
A fine is definitely in order,

34
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,759
but please don't make it so steep.

35
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,680
I'm just a nobody.

36
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,120
I can't afford to offend anyone.

37
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:15,560
Just reduce the fine a little.

38
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,680
Anyway, you host the dinner, I'll foot the bill.

39
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,560
Premium Kaoliang.

40
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,959
It's set for tonight.

41
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,120
Where's your pushy classmate?

42
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,399
She'll be half an hour late.

43
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,120
I'm the one who notified her.

44
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,160
This story is off to an interesting start.

45
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,519
Have a seat.

46
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,480
She quoted you 20 a person.

47
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,439
You doubled it to 40.

48
00:05:56,759 --> 00:05:58,639
But she only gave us 30 each.

49
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:01,240
You can come to me for any future events.

50
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,720
I'll find the people for you.

51
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,959
There are plenty of volunteers.

52
00:06:03,959 --> 00:06:05,399
We only ask for 35.

53
00:06:09,519 --> 00:06:11,480
We can go even lower.

54
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:11,959
I need to head back.

55
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:13,000
There won't be a next time.

56
00:06:13,399 --> 00:06:14,959
With you being so aggressive,

57
00:06:15,519 --> 00:06:16,920
who would ever hire you again?

58
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,319
People need to trust each other.

59
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:20,839
This partnership wasn't pleasant.

60
00:06:21,079 --> 00:06:22,480
Let's not talk business anymore.

61
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,720
Last time was an accident.

62
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,000
Taking your watch was...

63
00:06:34,079 --> 00:06:34,959
But on a personal level,

64
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,839
we're still friends.

65
00:06:42,839 --> 00:06:43,600
Open it and take a look.

66
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,319
If you like it,

67
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:50,399
I can give it to you.

68
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:57,839
Let me put it on for you.

69
00:06:59,519 --> 00:07:00,319
Turn around.

70
00:07:31,079 --> 00:07:31,879
It suits you.

71
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,680
Can I just not tell Jin Li'na?

72
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:39,680
That's up to you.

73
00:07:40,879 --> 00:07:41,680
Boss Lin.

74
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,160
Elder Lin.

75
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:48,879
You're here.

76
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:05,199
Professor Cao, Deputy Chief Engineer.

77
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,240
Congratulations, Professor Cao.

78
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:10,920
Congratulations on your promotion to Deputy Chief Engineer.

79
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,199
Congratulations.

80
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,360
You count it too.

81
00:08:27,519 --> 00:08:28,160
No need.

82
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,600
Boss Lin wouldn't cheat us.

83
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:32,000
If he meant to,

84
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,360
he wouldn't have called us.

85
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,320
The shoes.

86
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,840
And the sneakers.

87
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,879
Just like we agreed.

88
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:45,919
Right here.

89
00:08:46,279 --> 00:08:47,720
You already gave them to me before you came in.

90
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,879
Why are there only two pairs?

91
00:08:59,879 --> 00:09:00,720
What about the others?

92
00:09:01,159 --> 00:09:03,080
I only promised to give them to you two.

93
00:09:03,679 --> 00:09:04,799
Give one to everybody?

94
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:05,720
Am I crazy?

95
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,720
But that's not what you said before.

96
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:08,840
Jin Lina.

97
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,799
That's enough.

98
00:09:10,799 --> 00:09:12,720
How am I supposed to explain this to them?

99
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,039
Just give them the money.

100
00:09:14,039 --> 00:09:15,279
Maybe they forgot about it.

101
00:09:15,919 --> 00:09:17,279
You can call the police.

102
00:09:17,279 --> 00:09:18,519
You can call the cops over.

103
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:19,519
Let them be the judge.

104
00:09:25,759 --> 00:09:26,879
From now on, good or bad,

105
00:09:26,879 --> 00:09:28,480
put it all in the contract.

106
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:33,639
Let's go.

107
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:34,600
Wait a minute.

108
00:09:35,639 --> 00:09:36,440
What's wrong?

109
00:09:40,639 --> 00:09:42,000
Why are you looking at me?

110
00:09:42,679 --> 00:09:43,679
This isn't my watch.

111
00:09:44,159 --> 00:09:45,399
How can it not be your watch?

112
00:09:45,399 --> 00:09:46,519
This is your watch.

113
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,159
This is a fake.

114
00:09:52,799 --> 00:09:54,360
Now it's my turn to call the police.

115
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,200
Lu Zhifei! Lu Zhifei!

116
00:10:07,639 --> 00:10:09,039
I just went to Pacific.

117
00:10:09,039 --> 00:10:10,720
You weren't on comp time.

118
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,000
You took personal leave.

119
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,200
I also went to the place you rented.

120
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,000
Who was that waiting for you at the door?

121
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,720
He didn't look like a good guy.

122
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,480
Xiao Jiang has already gone back home.

123
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,720
Why did you guys lie to me?

124
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,200
What are you hiding from?

125
00:10:25,159 --> 00:10:26,200
I'm not hiding from anything!

126
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,879
You're still lying to me.

127
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:28,919
Then let me ask you.

128
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:30,000
Where's the watch?

129
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:34,240
Do you have any idea how much that watch is worth?

130
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:36,519
A hundred thousand yuan!

131
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:38,879
Now they want to press charges for theft.

132
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:41,080
You'll spend at least twenty years in prison.

133
00:10:41,639 --> 00:10:43,320
You'll rot in there, you idiot!

134
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:06,919
Some look like dates.

135
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,440
Others, I can't figure out.

136
00:11:08,639 --> 00:11:09,639
Where did you get this?

137
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,000
From an old cold case.

138
00:11:12,159 --> 00:11:13,360
Notes taken by a suspect.

139
00:11:14,279 --> 00:11:15,519
It is hard to guess.

140
00:11:15,519 --> 00:11:16,519
That's why it's a cold case.

141
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:17,759
There's no logic to it.

142
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:18,960
I can't analyze it.

143
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,320
What about the Provincial Department?

144
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,600
Do they have any other way?

145
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,639
There's no context,

146
00:11:22,639 --> 00:11:23,919
and no correlation.

147
00:11:23,919 --> 00:11:25,399
It makes absolutely no sense.

148
00:11:25,679 --> 00:11:26,440
No one can do anything about it.

149
00:11:28,919 --> 00:11:29,600
Chunxiao.

150
00:11:33,519 --> 00:11:35,559
No wonder I didn't see you just now.

151
00:11:35,559 --> 00:11:37,000
You came to Xiaowu to get something analyzed?

152
00:11:38,279 --> 00:11:40,440
Chief Wei said to go over all the Taiwan Strait cold cases.

153
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,200
There's too much stuff to analyze.

154
00:11:42,879 --> 00:11:43,720
Where are you going?

155
00:11:44,759 --> 00:11:45,960
My car keeps breaking down.

156
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,120
It has too many minor issues.

157
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,240
I'm going to the maintenance team.

158
00:11:50,879 --> 00:11:52,320
Your car still isn't fixed?

159
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:53,919
Didn't they say they couldn't find the problem?

160
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:55,639
That's just how I am.

161
00:11:55,639 --> 00:11:56,639
The harder it is to find the problem,

162
00:11:56,639 --> 00:11:58,600
the more I want to figure out what's wrong with it.

163
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,080
True.

164
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,679
It'll be easier to commute once it's fixed.

165
00:12:03,559 --> 00:12:04,919
I heard you rent your place.

166
00:12:07,799 --> 00:12:09,200
I don't want to live at home anymore either.

167
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,039
My mom nags too much.

168
00:12:10,519 --> 00:12:11,399
Did you find it yourself?

169
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,440
I asked door to door.

170
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,559
You can also ask the Neighborhood Committee.

171
00:12:14,559 --> 00:12:15,320
It's more convenient.

172
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,480
Which street do you live on?

173
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,320
Is it easy to get around?

174
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,480
What do you mean by a pawn agency?

175
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,320
Isn't it just a pawnshop?

176
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,600
Which one?

177
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:25,639
Not far from the station.

178
00:12:25,639 --> 00:12:27,200
The first one at the entrance of Dongxi Alley.

179
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,399
How much did they charge you?

180
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,960
The maximum renewal period is one month.

181
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,360
Plus an eight percent service fee.

182
00:12:32,759 --> 00:12:33,720
And after a month?

183
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,399
How will you pay it back?

184
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,240
Plus another 0.5 percent.

185
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,720
The sky isn't falling.

186
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,600
At worst, we borrow and pay it back together.

187
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,440
That would have worked.

188
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,919
Did you have to scam people with a fake watch?

189
00:12:44,919 --> 00:12:46,879
Don't you know if you dare to commit fraud now,

190
00:12:46,879 --> 00:12:48,799
you'll dare to kill tomorrow?

191
00:12:48,799 --> 00:12:51,039
Are the people who made you take photos forcing you?

192
00:12:51,039 --> 00:12:53,120
Are you really hiding from creditors?

193
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,200
Say something!

194
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:54,919
No, it's not like that.

195
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:56,360
It's the photo studio boss.

196
00:12:57,559 --> 00:12:59,519
I broke his Canon camera before.

197
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:00,759
And the camera got confiscated too.

198
00:13:00,759 --> 00:13:02,120
I can't drag my friend down with me.

199
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,879
What do you mean by dragging your friend down?

200
00:13:03,879 --> 00:13:05,200
Was the money you got from pawning not enough?

201
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,440
No, it wasn't.

202
00:13:07,639 --> 00:13:08,759
I have to help Xiaojiang cover his debts.

203
00:13:08,759 --> 00:13:10,240
I borrowed from a loan shark.

204
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:19,240
Auntie,

205
00:13:20,039 --> 00:13:20,879
well,

206
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,519
I want to discuss something with you.

207
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:24,600
Lina,

208
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,720
you don't have to agree.

209
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:34,720
A classmate at our school got sick.

210
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:37,080
So the school is organizing a loan.

211
00:13:38,679 --> 00:13:39,440
Right.

212
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,919
It's a loan, not a donation.

213
00:13:41,919 --> 00:13:44,720
They just want everyone to help out.

214
00:13:45,039 --> 00:13:47,919
And that classmate is in my dorm.

215
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:50,879
Alright.

216
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:51,759
Bye-bye.

217
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,879
Mr. Zhang, can I make another call?

218
00:14:21,879 --> 00:14:22,799
Go ahead, go ahead.

219
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,559
This is Jin Lina.

220
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,080
I just want to see you.

221
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,200
Are you free?

222
00:14:44,039 --> 00:14:45,080
Maybe tonight?

223
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,440
I want to borrow some money

224
00:14:49,799 --> 00:14:51,399
to get your watch back first.

225
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,600
I can write an IOU.

226
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,759
I can leave my fingerprint.

227
00:14:56,559 --> 00:14:57,799
I'll pay it back slowly.

228
00:15:01,559 --> 00:15:02,840
I can even pay interest.

229
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,440
If you need volunteers again in the future,

230
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,519
I'll help you find people.

231
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,159
I won't take any money myself.

232
00:15:20,679 --> 00:15:22,200
I'll leave my student ID with you.

233
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,840
You know where my school is.

234
00:15:23,919 --> 00:15:24,960
I can't run away.

235
00:15:38,759 --> 00:15:39,759
Where is your home?

236
00:15:39,759 --> 00:15:40,799
My hometown is in Sichuan.

237
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,919
I have relatives here too.

238
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,440
My aunt's house is right

239
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,399
in the military compound next to the weather station.

240
00:15:49,759 --> 00:15:50,720
The military, huh?

241
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,840
There are soldiers at the gate.

242
00:15:53,559 --> 00:15:54,840
Holding guns.

243
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,159
If you hide inside,

244
00:15:56,159 --> 00:15:57,360
how am I supposed to get in?

245
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,720
Then I'll agree to whatever you want.

246
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,519
You use my money

247
00:16:01,519 --> 00:16:02,600
to buy back my watch,

248
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:04,000
and expect me to owe you a favor.

249
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,279
And you tell me to find a way out.

250
00:16:05,399 --> 00:16:06,279
But I haven't even said

251
00:16:06,279 --> 00:16:07,639
if I'll call the cops on your boyfriend

252
00:16:07,639 --> 00:16:08,399
and have him sentenced.

253
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:09,759
He's just an idiot.

254
00:16:09,759 --> 00:16:12,200
He foolishly got mixed up with the wrong crowd.

255
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,039
He was supposed to come with me today

256
00:16:14,039 --> 00:16:15,080
to apologize to you.

257
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:17,480
But right before we left, he chickened out.

258
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,519
Actually, all of this is my fault.

259
00:16:19,519 --> 00:16:20,039
Even if you beat me to death,

260
00:16:20,039 --> 00:16:21,960
I had no idea this watch was so expensive.

261
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:23,000
If I had known,

262
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:23,759
Stand up.

263
00:16:41,279 --> 00:16:42,639
Turn around and let me see.

264
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,960
What do you want?

265
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,000
A work-study job.

266
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:55,360
Have you considered it?

267
00:16:59,759 --> 00:17:00,879
You're too thin.

268
00:17:01,159 --> 00:17:02,360
And you don't wear makeup.

269
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,759
But you have a decent foundation.

270
00:17:03,759 --> 00:17:04,480
If you clean up a bit,

271
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,920
you'll be presentable enough to take out.

272
00:17:06,559 --> 00:17:07,960
I'll hire you as my secretary.

273
00:17:08,359 --> 00:17:09,559
You don't have to work every day.

274
00:17:09,759 --> 00:17:11,359
When I need you,

275
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:13,079
just take time off from school.

276
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:14,119
Your salary will be paid monthly,

277
00:17:14,119 --> 00:17:15,240
with a year-end bonus.

278
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:16,359
How does that sound?

279
00:17:17,559 --> 00:17:18,640
What do you mean?

280
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:21,160
I'll redeem the watch myself.

281
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,599
Consider the money a loan for now.

282
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:24,440
Pay me back when you've saved up your wages.

283
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,200
It's better than not getting my old debt back,

284
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,759
and having to give you even more money.

285
00:17:29,839 --> 00:17:30,640
Okay.

286
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,440
But can I...

287
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,200
get a month's salary in advance?

288
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,599
Are you always this shameless?

289
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:45,720
Xiao Lu still has to pay for the camera.

290
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:49,200
His friend owes loan sharks and needs cash fast.

291
00:17:50,079 --> 00:17:52,200
Why didn't you ask how much your salary is?

292
00:17:52,519 --> 00:17:54,079
No matter how much it is,

293
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,559
I couldn't ask for a two-month advance.

294
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,079
I wouldn't have the nerve.

295
00:17:59,359 --> 00:18:02,039
I find you quite interesting.

296
00:18:04,319 --> 00:18:05,920
Then, as your secretary,

297
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,200
what will I be doing?

298
00:18:08,559 --> 00:18:09,559
First, a trip to Beijing.

299
00:18:09,559 --> 00:18:10,519
To discuss some business.

300
00:18:10,759 --> 00:18:11,920
When?

301
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,119
Wait for my word.

302
00:18:18,039 --> 00:18:19,160
Maybe tomorrow.

303
00:18:19,759 --> 00:18:20,799
Maybe the day after.

304
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:26,440
Eat up. It's quite good.

305
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,240
How is it?

306
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,319
Delicious.

307
00:18:57,799 --> 00:18:58,960
The car's gone.

308
00:18:58,960 --> 00:18:59,960
Why are you still taking pictures?

309
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,720
Let's go. Time to go home.

310
00:19:11,559 --> 00:19:13,200
Why won't it start again?

311
00:19:13,599 --> 00:19:15,119
Wasn't it just fixed earlier today?

312
00:19:15,839 --> 00:19:17,599
The maintenance crew can never fix it right.

313
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:18,599
How about this?

314
00:19:18,599 --> 00:19:20,279
I'll drive it to the repair shop in a bit.

315
00:19:20,279 --> 00:19:21,839
I just don't know what time they get off work.

316
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:27,279
Might as well let it break completely.

317
00:19:27,599 --> 00:19:28,839
Once it gets to the point where it can't be fixed,

318
00:19:28,839 --> 00:19:29,759
there'll be no need to fix it anymore.

319
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,279
What do you mean?

320
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,319
By the way, Uncle,

321
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,200
Second Grandpa said

322
00:19:41,319 --> 00:19:42,799
those of us who have regular jobs

323
00:19:42,799 --> 00:19:44,240
don't need to go back this time.

324
00:19:44,559 --> 00:19:46,599
Wait until the ancestral hall is fully renovated,

325
00:19:46,599 --> 00:19:48,119
we'll pick a date,

326
00:19:48,119 --> 00:19:49,079
and then go back together.

327
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:52,680
Originally, they wanted you to host it,

328
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:54,920
but I said you had to go to Beijing to meet the leaders.

329
00:19:55,799 --> 00:19:57,319
It's a matter of bringing honor to our ancestors.

330
00:19:57,319 --> 00:19:58,880
Our ancestors will understand.

331
00:19:59,319 --> 00:20:01,720
Just take whatever money is needed from the cabinet.

332
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,000
Wait a while,

333
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,200
and you can take it down to the countryside.

334
00:20:05,119 --> 00:20:05,920
Okay.

335
00:20:08,039 --> 00:20:08,480
Step aside.

336
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,279
Let me do it.

337
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:16,960
Uncle,

338
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,079
this time, is Mayor Xie

339
00:20:20,079 --> 00:20:21,240
going with you?

340
00:20:21,759 --> 00:20:22,759
It's not government business.

341
00:20:22,759 --> 00:20:23,960
Why would he go?

342
00:20:25,519 --> 00:20:27,240
I... I was thinking,

343
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:27,920
look,

344
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,960
I've been at the Sports Bureau for so many years.

345
00:20:30,079 --> 00:20:31,480
Always jumping around there,

346
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,599
it's not very interesting.

347
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,119
I want to transfer

348
00:20:35,519 --> 00:20:36,440
to a better department.

349
00:20:39,559 --> 00:20:42,000
I just draw blueprints and do math.

350
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,039
These things...

351
00:20:43,359 --> 00:20:44,720
I'm afraid I really can't say them.

352
00:20:45,079 --> 00:20:47,359
Aren't you about to be promoted to Deputy Chief Engineer?

353
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,240
When you come back from Beijing,

354
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,960
the leaders will definitely meet you.

355
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,279
If you get close to them,

356
00:20:52,359 --> 00:20:53,759
it just takes a single word.

357
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,559
You should first get your professional title

358
00:20:57,559 --> 00:20:58,960
sorted out.

359
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,680
How many times have I told you?

360
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,000
You just won't listen to me.

361
00:21:02,279 --> 00:21:04,279
If the leaders really ask about it,

362
00:21:04,279 --> 00:21:06,279
won't they still ask about your own qualifications?

363
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:11,200
I don't think the others have such great qualifications.

364
00:21:15,359 --> 00:21:18,759
Uncle, you need to speak up about this.

365
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:22,839
Anyway, I think Aunt is right.

366
00:21:23,839 --> 00:21:25,279
You can't be too shy.

367
00:21:25,279 --> 00:21:26,599
If you don't tell anyone,

368
00:21:26,599 --> 00:21:28,319
no one will offer to help you.

369
00:21:28,319 --> 00:21:29,799
Just like this time with your housing allocation,

370
00:21:29,799 --> 00:21:30,880
you have to speak up.

371
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,079
Not only do you have to speak up,

372
00:21:32,079 --> 00:21:34,039
you should also visit the leaders' homes.

373
00:21:34,039 --> 00:21:35,240
That's completely unnecessary.

374
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:38,200
How can a Deputy Chief Engineer not have an apartment?

375
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,559
Use common sense.

376
00:21:39,559 --> 00:21:40,680
It's just like Zhuge Liang

377
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,759
not believing Sima Yi would enter the city.

378
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:45,319
Why put on a show if you aren't confident?

379
00:21:45,319 --> 00:21:46,279
That's just an opera.

380
00:21:47,279 --> 00:21:49,640
I just don't believe Sima Yi wouldn't dare enter the city.

381
00:22:06,839 --> 00:22:07,640
Would he dare?

382
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,759
It's a deadly trap where you'll lose your head.

383
00:22:14,839 --> 00:22:15,400
Director.

384
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,640
I'm off the clock, Section Chief Wei.

385
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:19,839
You're late.

386
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,480
If it's business, it can wait until tomorrow.

387
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,279
Don't bother if it's trivial.

388
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:24,599
I have important business with you.

389
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:27,039
When is it ever not important with you?

390
00:22:27,319 --> 00:22:28,119
Let's go. Come on.

391
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,079
Let's go inside. It's classified.

392
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,200
I'm here to "bribe" you.

393
00:22:35,359 --> 00:22:36,240
Your "bribe", huh?

394
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:38,920
It better be good.

395
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,240
Guaranteed to satisfy.

396
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:42,640
Today is my mother-in-law's birthday.

397
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,759
If it were my own mother's birthday,

398
00:22:45,839 --> 00:22:47,240
being late wouldn't be a big deal.

399
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:49,920
Requesting a replacement vehicle.

400
00:22:51,279 --> 00:22:52,599
Section 2's Santana is broken.

401
00:22:52,599 --> 00:22:53,799
The engine is leaking.

402
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:55,839
Alright.

403
00:22:56,599 --> 00:22:57,200
Get in line.

404
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,599
I have a reason to cut the line.

405
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:01,279
Recruitment attempts have noticeably increased lately.

406
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:02,400
The methods are endless.

407
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:04,240
There's a relative of a military officer.

408
00:23:04,519 --> 00:23:07,160
This girl is a student at the teachers' college.

409
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:08,079
Her aunt,

410
00:23:08,079 --> 00:23:09,240
although not high in rank,

411
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:11,480
holds a very crucial position and status.

412
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:13,160
Her uncle works near the military compound,

413
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,400
at a local hospital.

414
00:23:14,519 --> 00:23:15,559
Although he has no military status,

415
00:23:15,559 --> 00:23:16,559
he can easily

416
00:23:16,559 --> 00:23:17,920
come into contact with military personnel.

417
00:23:22,759 --> 00:23:24,359
This guy is a Taiwanese businessman.

418
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,799
On the day the "Postman" was arrested,

419
00:23:25,799 --> 00:23:27,319
he was seen at the crime scene.

420
00:23:27,599 --> 00:23:28,559
Also, rumor has it

421
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,079
that he'll be leaving Minzhong soon.

422
00:23:30,319 --> 00:23:31,880
If he's heading to Beijing,

423
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,799
just like the guest coming from Taipei,

424
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,359
then things get interesting.

425
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,319
Lin Kanshan.

426
00:23:38,759 --> 00:23:39,359
Right.

427
00:23:41,119 --> 00:23:42,319
Seeing a mountain as a mountain,

428
00:23:42,559 --> 00:23:43,640
seeing a mountain as not a mountain.

429
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:44,799
Interesting.

430
00:23:46,119 --> 00:23:47,079
Requesting to open a case.

431
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,559
We need a car to tail him.

432
00:23:48,559 --> 00:23:49,400
I want a new car

433
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:50,319
assigned to Section 2.

434
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:51,480
Before work tomorrow morning,

435
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:52,400
have it ready for us.

436
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,039
Thank you, Director.

437
00:23:54,799 --> 00:23:56,039
Institutes 761 and 766

438
00:23:56,039 --> 00:23:57,839
have overlapping schedules for Beijing.

439
00:23:57,839 --> 00:24:00,039
Now we have the magnet.

440
00:24:00,759 --> 00:24:02,440
The only thing I haven't figured out

441
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:04,319
is who to assign as his lead tail.

442
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,160
Who do you want to send?

443
00:24:10,799 --> 00:24:12,440
Mutton hotpot, sweet garlic.

444
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:14,000
The standard set.

445
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:16,079
Cabbage, glass noodles, tofu.

446
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,359
And that sesame paste flatbread.

447
00:24:24,319 --> 00:24:24,640
Hello.

448
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:25,640
Hello. Where are you heading?

449
00:24:26,359 --> 00:24:27,240
Beijing.

450
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,200
Please show your IDs.

451
00:24:29,119 --> 00:24:29,880
Taiwanese compatriot.

452
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:30,519
For two.

453
00:24:30,759 --> 00:24:32,160
Please show the other ID.

454
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:33,359
Your ID.

455
00:24:39,319 --> 00:24:41,039
Hard to tell which of us is the secretary.

456
00:24:41,759 --> 00:24:43,000
I'll know the drill next time.

457
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:44,880
That'll be one thousand yuan for two.

458
00:24:48,839 --> 00:24:50,359
Please check your luggage.

459
00:24:51,559 --> 00:24:53,039
Put your luggage here.

460
00:25:02,759 --> 00:25:03,920
Here are your tickets and IDs.

461
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:04,640
Have a pleasant journey.

462
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:05,440
Thanks.

463
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:07,160
Then take dried shrimp,

464
00:25:07,359 --> 00:25:08,440
and toss them in.

465
00:25:09,559 --> 00:25:10,799
Can you even call that mutton hotpot anymore?

466
00:25:10,799 --> 00:25:12,359
That's how they do it in the Northeast.

467
00:25:14,079 --> 00:25:15,079
Just like the rich guys.

468
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:17,440
Some wear gold bracelets.

469
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:20,960
They're just copying Hong Kongers and...

470
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,000
Hello.

471
00:25:22,079 --> 00:25:22,960
Two tickets to Beijing.

472
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:23,680
Okay.

473
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:27,279
Here.

474
00:25:29,359 --> 00:25:30,240
Have a pleasant journey.

475
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,079
Thank you.

476
00:25:31,079 --> 00:25:31,839
You're welcome.

477
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:34,440
Come, come.

478
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:54,440
Let's not meet again once we get to Beijing.

479
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:14,440
Here are some mooncakes for you.

480
00:26:14,839 --> 00:26:15,839
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

481
00:26:15,839 --> 00:26:16,839
Wishing you good health.

482
00:26:16,839 --> 00:26:18,839
Chief Hao, we brought you mooncakes.

483
00:26:18,839 --> 00:26:20,920
Your favorite, Yongding mooncakes.

484
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,240
Can your teeth still chew them?

485
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:23,559
He can't hear you.

486
00:26:23,839 --> 00:26:25,200
He couldn't even chew them last year.

487
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:26,279
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

488
00:26:26,279 --> 00:26:27,680
Wishing you good health.

489
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:28,599
Thanks. Thank you.

490
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:29,440
Here.

491
00:26:29,599 --> 00:26:30,799
You need to get those teeth fixed.

492
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:31,960
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

493
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:33,200
Wishing you good health.

494
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,160
Auntie Li.

495
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:35,640
Xiao Wu.

496
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,359
How are your eyes doing?

497
00:26:37,359 --> 00:26:39,039
Can you see the news broadcast clearly?

498
00:26:39,039 --> 00:26:40,119
Keep your voice down.

499
00:26:40,119 --> 00:26:41,000
I can hear you.

500
00:26:42,359 --> 00:26:44,599
Auntie Li, mooncakes for you.

501
00:26:45,599 --> 00:26:46,759
When Auntie Li was young,

502
00:26:46,759 --> 00:26:48,000
she had the eyes of a hawk.

503
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,279
Anyone trying to sneak in from the other side

504
00:26:49,279 --> 00:26:50,240
through the sea,

505
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:51,279
no matter how dark it was,

506
00:26:51,279 --> 00:26:52,799
Auntie Li could spot them at a glance.

507
00:26:52,799 --> 00:26:53,759
Right, Auntie Li?

508
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,839
Auntie Li, Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

509
00:26:55,839 --> 00:26:56,839
Wishing you good health.

510
00:26:58,039 --> 00:26:58,960
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

511
00:27:05,039 --> 00:27:06,000
To be honest, even today,

512
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,440
I still feel intimidated when I see her.

513
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,680
When I was young and talked to her,

514
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:10,920
I didn't even dare to look her in the eye.

515
00:27:11,119 --> 00:27:11,839
She's that fierce?

516
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:15,359
We're both from Lianjiang County.

517
00:27:16,799 --> 00:27:17,720
Back then,

518
00:27:18,279 --> 00:27:19,759
Dinghai Bay was still called Spy Island.

519
00:27:19,759 --> 00:27:21,279
Right across the sea was Matsu Island.

520
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:23,160
Those who sneaked in from Taiwan, China,

521
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:25,000
basically all landed in Lianjiang County.

522
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:28,039
Auntie Li was a militia company commander in her youth.

523
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:29,920
Once, she caught

524
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:30,599
a covert squad claiming they would

525
00:27:30,599 --> 00:27:32,680
"counterattack the mainland."

526
00:27:33,559 --> 00:27:36,119
There were about 30 or 40 of them.

527
00:27:36,759 --> 00:27:37,559
They arrested them overnight,

528
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:39,200
capturing both the men and their weapons.

529
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,160
Not a single one escaped.

530
00:27:40,519 --> 00:27:42,640
They even seized a small radio transmitter.

531
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:43,920
She kept it at home instead of turning it in,

532
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:44,799
claiming it was her trophy.

533
00:27:45,799 --> 00:27:47,920
When I first got here, she had just retired.

534
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:48,680
I heard that

535
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:49,480
she had a terrible temper

536
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:50,559
and would scold anyone she caught.

537
00:27:50,559 --> 00:27:51,400
She'd curse in her dialect.

538
00:27:52,039 --> 00:27:52,799
If you provoked her,

539
00:27:52,799 --> 00:27:54,000
she'd chew you out completely.

540
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:58,079
She had seniority, merits, and authority.

541
00:27:58,680 --> 00:27:59,960
She was also my mentor.

542
00:28:00,519 --> 00:28:01,680
A strict master trains a skilled apprentice.

543
00:28:01,839 --> 00:28:03,799
Without her, you wouldn't be my mentor either.

544
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:06,440
Your skilled apprentice has set off by now, right?

545
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:08,680
Ma Qi and He Chunxiao.

546
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:10,160
How are they doing?

547
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,559
Trust those you use, and don't use those you doubt.

548
00:28:11,839 --> 00:28:12,599
You taught me that.

549
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:15,559
From Taiwan, China, to here,

550
00:28:16,279 --> 00:28:17,359
and from here to Beijing.

551
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:20,000
That's quite a big detour.

552
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,559
Representatives from over a dozen research institutes

553
00:28:22,559 --> 00:28:24,400
are all heading to Beijing to receive awards.

554
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:26,160
Aerospace, missiles, fuels...

555
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:28,400
All the prime targets are gathered there.

556
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,440
If I were a demon,

557
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:30,799
I'd come down the mountain for a bite too.

558
00:28:31,279 --> 00:28:32,599
All departments have deployed agents.

559
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:34,960
Every single target must be well protected.

560
00:28:36,599 --> 00:28:38,599
What's your analysis on Lin Kanshan?

561
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:41,400
Who is he acting as a middleman for in Beijing this time?

562
00:28:42,400 --> 00:28:43,799
It's still unclear.

563
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:45,559
Right now,

564
00:28:45,559 --> 00:28:46,799
we can only suspect the thief,

565
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,960
but we don't know who the victim is yet.

566
00:28:48,960 --> 00:28:51,519
We have no choice but to keep an eye on Lin Kanshan,

567
00:28:51,519 --> 00:28:52,799
and wait for the gathered intel.

568
00:28:55,759 --> 00:28:57,720
Just a Monkey King and his little sidekick...

569
00:28:58,640 --> 00:28:59,599
Beijing is so big.

570
00:28:59,599 --> 00:29:00,680
Can they keep an eye on the demon?

571
00:29:09,359 --> 00:29:10,599
This morning, right?

572
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,559
Real name or anonymous?

573
00:29:15,519 --> 00:29:17,200
Engineer Cao? He's right next to me.

574
00:29:17,799 --> 00:29:19,400
Yes, yes. We just arrived in Beijing.

575
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:21,079
Alright, alright.

576
00:29:21,599 --> 00:29:22,440
Got it.

577
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:25,000
Who was that?

578
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:25,680
What is it?

579
00:29:27,079 --> 00:29:28,599
It's about your promotion to Deputy Chief Engineer.

580
00:29:28,599 --> 00:29:29,720
There's a bit of a problem.

581
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:33,400
What problem?

582
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,359
A problem with me?

583
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,359
Does someone have an issue with me?

584
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,400
I don't have the details yet.

585
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:41,400
Don't get anxious just yet.

586
00:29:41,839 --> 00:29:43,559
The organization will investigate thoroughly.

587
00:29:45,079 --> 00:29:46,680
If they have an issue, they should use their real name.

588
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:47,920
Have them come to me.

589
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,680
I'll talk to them face to face.

590
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:02,480
Chairman Mao

591
00:30:18,599 --> 00:30:20,000
It's really big.

592
00:30:51,799 --> 00:30:52,599
Let me.

593
00:30:53,079 --> 00:30:54,160
Give it to me.

594
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,119
Give me the IDs.

595
00:31:17,519 --> 00:31:18,279
Have a nice day.

596
00:31:18,279 --> 00:31:18,880
Thank you.

597
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:19,720
This way.

598
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,480
Welcome.

599
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:24,240
Hello, we have a reservation.

600
00:31:24,519 --> 00:31:25,319
For two.

601
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:26,240
How many nights?

602
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:29,720
Boss, how many nights are we staying?

603
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:31,160
Two nights for now.

604
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:33,160
Do we get a discount for staying two nights in a row?

605
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:33,759
I'm sorry.

606
00:31:33,759 --> 00:31:34,440
We don't offer any discounts here.

607
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:35,680
Alright, just check us in.

608
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:36,440
Hurry up.

609
00:31:38,799 --> 00:31:39,559
Wait a minute.

610
00:31:39,559 --> 00:31:41,559
What's that member rate about?

611
00:31:41,559 --> 00:31:42,559
Are we members?

612
00:31:43,119 --> 00:31:44,839
Can you keep your voice down?

613
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:50,079
How many rooms?

614
00:31:50,079 --> 00:31:50,599
Two rooms.

615
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:03,519
Thank you, boss.

616
00:32:05,519 --> 00:32:07,599
This hotel feels so big.

617
00:32:15,559 --> 00:32:16,799
Boss, this way, this way.

618
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,359
My goodness.

619
00:32:19,359 --> 00:32:20,640
Can you let me out, please?

620
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:21,279
I'm sorry.

621
00:32:21,279 --> 00:32:21,960
I didn't mean to.

622
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:22,960
Sorry, sorry.

623
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:23,599
You're in my way.

624
00:32:23,599 --> 00:32:24,720
Just be more careful.

625
00:32:24,920 --> 00:32:25,759
Alright, that's enough.

626
00:32:25,759 --> 00:32:26,400
I'm sorry.

627
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,400
My goodness.

628
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:28,480
Just be more careful.

629
00:32:29,319 --> 00:32:31,039
It was her suitcase blocking the way.

630
00:32:31,039 --> 00:32:32,359
Alright, that's enough.

631
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:35,960
She's used to being bossy.

632
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,640
Help me find my slippers.

633
00:33:29,559 --> 00:33:30,680
In the restroom.

634
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,119
Found it.

635
00:33:37,880 --> 00:33:38,440
Here.

636
00:33:42,759 --> 00:33:43,599
Make a pot of tea.

637
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:44,480
Okay.

638
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:52,880
Boss, there's no water in this kettle.

639
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:54,079
I'll go boil some for you.

640
00:33:54,079 --> 00:33:54,599
Wait a minute.

641
00:33:57,039 --> 00:33:57,599
Come here.

642
00:34:02,559 --> 00:34:03,519
Come here and sit.

643
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,119
What for?

644
00:34:10,159 --> 00:34:11,559
What do you think a secretary does?

645
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:13,880
Massage my shoulders.

646
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:14,960
Rub my lower back.

647
00:34:15,360 --> 00:34:16,719
I'm tired from the long car ride.

648
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:18,000
Come here.

649
00:34:21,159 --> 00:34:22,079
Just come here.

650
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:25,440
What do you think I'm trying to do?

651
00:34:25,440 --> 00:34:26,559
I pay your salary,

652
00:34:26,559 --> 00:34:28,400
pay for your flights and hotels.

653
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:29,679
I spend so much money.

654
00:34:29,679 --> 00:34:31,719
If I wanted to be a creep, I wouldn't have picked you.

655
00:34:31,719 --> 00:34:33,119
What on earth are you thinking?

656
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:37,519
Unbelievable.

657
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,440
What are you looking at?

658
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,199
Go, go, get out.

659
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,639
Like a block of wood.

660
00:35:17,599 --> 00:35:19,599
I can't get into my room.

661
00:35:38,239 --> 00:35:40,119
Just pick up the receiver to monitor.

662
00:35:42,519 --> 00:35:44,280
If you want drinks, call for them yourself.

663
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,840
Someone will bring them up to you.

664
00:35:46,840 --> 00:35:47,360
Brother Qi.

665
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:48,840
You can really hear the voices from upstairs.

666
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:49,480
Loud and clear.

667
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:51,320
You're not even on a phone call.

668
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:52,639
Covering it so God doesn't hear?

669
00:35:54,079 --> 00:35:54,760
Back in basic training,

670
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:56,280
didn't Wu Jiali train you guys?

671
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:58,320
Who installed this equipment?

672
00:35:58,639 --> 00:36:00,199
Look at the Beijing Bureau's gear.

673
00:36:00,199 --> 00:36:01,360
Then look at ours.

674
00:36:01,599 --> 00:36:02,760
Were there other comrades?

675
00:36:03,199 --> 00:36:04,440
You think this is a movie?

676
00:36:05,199 --> 00:36:06,360
One person tailing one car?

677
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,559
With so many of our comrades around,

678
00:36:07,559 --> 00:36:08,480
you didn't spot a single one.

679
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:13,679
We work in three shifts.

680
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,280
You take the first shift.

681
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:17,360
Wake me if you hear anything interesting.

682
00:36:20,239 --> 00:36:21,199
Open the door.

683
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,719
The bathrobes and iron are inside.

684
00:36:23,719 --> 00:36:24,599
Now look over here.

685
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,000
The hair dryer is in that bag.

686
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,119
Do you know how to turn on the TV?

687
00:36:29,119 --> 00:36:29,760
I do.

688
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:31,440
Call the front desk if you need anything.

689
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:32,239
We're paying for this.

690
00:36:32,239 --> 00:36:33,679
Stop asking me over and over again.

691
00:36:35,159 --> 00:36:35,599
By the way, boss.

692
00:36:35,599 --> 00:36:37,679
I still need to ask you something.

693
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:38,840
For the next few days,

694
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:40,440
do we have any plans?

695
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:41,840
Do I need to prepare in advance?

696
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:43,360
We rest first.

697
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:44,559
Then we'll go sightseeing.

698
00:36:44,559 --> 00:36:46,440
And I'll take you for hot pot, okay?

699
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:48,519
Hard to tell who the secretary is here.

700
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:53,480
Does this monitor only pick up

701
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,039
this female student's room?

702
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,559
Can we hear Lin Kanshan's room?

703
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:11,719
Is this the front desk?

704
00:37:12,119 --> 00:37:13,239
I wanted to ask...

705
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:14,400
how to get to Wangfujing?

706
00:37:14,679 --> 00:37:15,519
What did you hear?

707
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,000
Brother Qi.

708
00:37:17,119 --> 00:37:19,039
How do you fall asleep and wake up just like that?

709
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:21,000
What did you hear?

710
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,920
He asked the front desk how to get to Wangfujing.

711
00:37:25,400 --> 00:37:26,440
He seems to be heading out now.

712
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:27,320
What's our move?

713
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:30,840
It's dry in Beijing.

714
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,599
Drink more water.

715
00:37:31,599 --> 00:37:31,840
Okay.

716
00:37:31,840 --> 00:37:32,280
Let's move.

717
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:57,079
Are there any vantage points when tailing someone?

718
00:37:57,079 --> 00:37:58,199
What do you mean by a vantage point?

719
00:37:58,199 --> 00:37:59,840
A place where I can hide myself,

720
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:00,840
and still keep an eye on him.

721
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:02,000
Is there a specific spot like that?

722
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,880
If you find a sweet spot like that, let me know.

723
00:38:04,199 --> 00:38:05,320
The first rule of tailing

724
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:06,840
is never treat your target like a fool.

725
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:09,280
If you think it's a good spot, so will they.

726
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:11,119
They'll look for the same spots you do.

727
00:38:11,119 --> 00:38:11,840
So you have to adapt.

728
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:12,880
Be unpredictable.

729
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:14,159
Forget what the textbooks say.

730
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:15,840
Forget about any bullshit vantage points.

731
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:17,400
Look ahead. Watch the target.

732
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:18,400
Rely on yourself.

733
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,599
Candied hawthorns!

734
00:38:44,599 --> 00:38:45,880
The simplest way

735
00:38:46,159 --> 00:38:47,519
is to not let him spot you.

736
00:38:49,559 --> 00:38:50,440
Memorize the layout.

737
00:38:50,519 --> 00:38:51,840
Stay out of his sight as much as possible.

738
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,519
Take a shortcut

739
00:38:52,719 --> 00:38:53,960
and wait for him on the other side.

740
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,000
Have you been to Beijing before?

741
00:38:58,239 --> 00:38:59,480
You know this place so well.

742
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:14,159
Excuse me, buddy.

743
00:39:15,199 --> 00:39:16,440
Alright, thank you.

744
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:18,800
Tanghulu!

745
00:39:23,239 --> 00:39:25,400
Tanghulu!

746
00:40:13,159 --> 00:40:14,639
All right, where we are right now

747
00:40:14,639 --> 00:40:16,880
is the core building of the Forbidden City,

748
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,920
the Hall of Supreme Harmony.

749
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,159
This Hall of Supreme Harmony

750
00:40:19,159 --> 00:40:22,119
is the largest palace in the Forbidden City.

751
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:24,599
All right, let's come over here and take a look.

752
00:40:24,599 --> 00:40:25,920
Now, our Hall of Supreme Harmony

753
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:28,920
is not just the largest palace in the Forbidden City...

754
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:29,840
Come on, come on!

755
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,679
Hurry up!

756
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:31,840
Come over for a picture!

757
00:40:32,639 --> 00:40:33,280
Three...

758
00:40:33,599 --> 00:40:34,280
Two...

759
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,960
Excuse me, excuse me.

760
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:37,960
Cheese!

761
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:40,119
Brother Qi,

762
00:40:41,280 --> 00:40:42,159
I need to use the restroom.

763
00:40:42,159 --> 00:40:43,079
Is there a toilet around?

764
00:40:44,599 --> 00:40:45,760
Do you know what a hand-drawn map is?

765
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:47,559
What is a hand-drawn map?

766
00:40:48,079 --> 00:40:49,280
Candied hawthorn!

767
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:51,840
Sweet and crispy candied hawthorn!

768
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:52,880
How much for one?

769
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:53,440
Fifty cents a skewer.

770
00:40:53,440 --> 00:40:54,440
One yuan for two.

771
00:40:54,559 --> 00:40:55,079
I'll take two.

772
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:56,239
All right, take your pick.

773
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:56,599
Okay.

774
00:40:56,719 --> 00:40:58,239
A map is dead, it's outdated.

775
00:40:58,239 --> 00:40:59,920
A hand-drawn one is alive, in real-time.

776
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:01,239
Whether in Minzhong or Beijing,

777
00:41:01,239 --> 00:41:02,840
navigating alleys or walking the main streets,

778
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:04,719
you must be familiar with every inch of the place.

779
00:41:04,719 --> 00:41:06,159
At least more familiar than your opponent.

780
00:41:06,159 --> 00:41:07,679
At least familiar enough that you don't need to look around

781
00:41:07,679 --> 00:41:09,000
to know where the toilet is.

782
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:09,840
Where is it?

783
00:41:10,079 --> 00:41:11,000
Is there one nearby?

784
00:41:11,679 --> 00:41:13,039
We passed one two minutes ago.

785
00:41:14,719 --> 00:41:15,519
Don't bother looking.

786
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,480
There's a long line of tourists at the door.

787
00:41:17,480 --> 00:41:18,679
You'd wet your pants before it's your turn.

788
00:41:19,079 --> 00:41:20,199
If you had a hand-drawn map,

789
00:41:20,199 --> 00:41:20,920
the first thing you'd do

790
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:22,079
is mark all the public toilets

791
00:41:22,079 --> 00:41:23,000
on it.

792
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:25,320
The key to tailing isn't just vantage points,

793
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,119
but also toilets.

794
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:28,239
A bladder is like a flour sack.

795
00:41:28,239 --> 00:41:29,400
It expands the longer you hold it in.

796
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:30,920
Remember,

797
00:41:31,039 --> 00:41:31,840
if you're heading out to tail someone,

798
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,840
drink less water from now on.

799
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,199
How do you know

800
00:41:34,519 --> 00:41:36,280
whether this guest who's never been to Beijing

801
00:41:36,280 --> 00:41:37,599
is going back to the hotel next,

802
00:41:37,599 --> 00:41:38,719
or heading to the Great Wall?

803
00:41:38,719 --> 00:41:39,960
But when you left,

804
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:41,480
didn't you drink hot tea too?

805
00:41:41,480 --> 00:41:42,480
I didn't drink any.

806
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:43,639
I poured that for you.

807
00:42:03,880 --> 00:42:05,639
You can't let a full bladder kill you.

808
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:07,400
Just pee your pants if you can't hold it.

809
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,280
Even a one-year-old knows that.

810
00:42:08,280 --> 00:42:09,440
And you still don't get it.

811
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:10,840
Brother Qi.

812
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:13,599
What is it?

813
00:42:14,679 --> 00:42:15,159
No...

814
00:42:15,159 --> 00:42:16,079
We're at the hotel.

815
00:42:30,159 --> 00:42:31,079
All the dishes are served.

816
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,079
Taipei has a Palace Museum,

817
00:42:34,079 --> 00:42:35,360
and there's one here too.

818
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:36,480
But there's no comparison.

819
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:38,000
Everything is just bigger on the mainland.

820
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:39,599
The tour guide told me

821
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:40,880
that many rooms inside the Palace Museum

822
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:41,840
aren't even open to the public.

823
00:42:41,840 --> 00:42:43,239
My legs are numb from all the walking,

824
00:42:43,239 --> 00:42:44,440
and we haven't even seen half of it.

825
00:42:46,519 --> 00:42:48,639
Think about where you want to go tomorrow.

826
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:49,440
Boss,

827
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:52,599
did you hire me just to travel with you?

828
00:42:53,039 --> 00:42:54,360
There are many types of secretaries.

829
00:42:54,840 --> 00:42:55,760
You're the most clueless one.

830
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:58,079
Nothing comes for free.

831
00:42:58,679 --> 00:43:00,719
Do you know which business is the most profitable right now?

832
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:03,039
Military enterprises.

833
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,119
I'm Wang Kai,

834
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,840
inviting you to watch the TV drama

835
00:43:11,119 --> 00:43:11,840
"Confrontation."

836
00:43:12,079 --> 00:43:14,199
Who do you think he's here to make contact with?

837
00:43:14,199 --> 00:43:15,239
I have a feeling

838
00:43:15,239 --> 00:43:16,480
he's not here to make contact.

839
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:17,519
It's a smokescreen.

840
00:43:26,320 --> 00:43:27,559
There's a coat on the bar.

